On the shell, yoyo watch now only does things that can actually happen. Everything else is refused with exit 2 (commit c8c0dc67, "Fixes #1088"). Build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all passed.

What I found first. I ran every form on the old binary, in an empty temp dir and in this repo:

| form | before | verdict | now |
|---|---|---|---|
| watch (command detected) | "Watch mode ON — 2 phases", exit 0 | false | refused, exit 2 |
| watch (nothing detected) | usage text, exit 2 | honest | same refusal as every other form, exit 2 |
| watch "echo hi" | "ON — will run…", exit 0 | false | refused, exit 2 |
| watch off | "Watch mode OFF", exit 0, though it was never on | false | refused, exit 2 |
| watch lint / all | same as bare watch | false | refused, exit 2 |
| watch status | "Watch mode: OFF", exit 0, even though this repo's .yoyo.toml has auto_watch = true | misleading | true report, exit 0 |

What the refusal says (on stderr, same shape and exit code as yoyo extended):
• The exact /watch … line to type inside a session. Passing one quoted argument still gives one command line.
• What auto_watch = true would do. I checked arm_auto_watch before writing this: it arms the detected command and takes no command of its own. So the message names the detected command, or says none was detected.
• For off, it says to leave auto_watch false instead.

watch status now says nothing is on in this process. It also says what auto_watch would do in a session started here, covering the same cases arm_auto_watch handles: off, nothing detected, tool not on PATH, armed.

Where the code went. The logic is in a new src/watch_shell.rs with table tests, called from the shell arm in dispatch_sub.rs. The REPL /watch path is untouched and its watch.rs tests are green and unedited.

Tests. One existing integration test asserted the false behaviour ("Watch mode ON", exit 0), so I rewrote it to assert the refusal. It still checks the quoting rules (through the /watch … line in the message) and that status exits 0. A second new test covers a detected Cargo project. To confirm they catch the bug, I put the old call back: both tests failed by name, and both passed again once I restored the fix.

Docs. Updated the commands.md table row and exit-code paragraph, plus the shell help line in src/help.rs, which still said "Toggle watch mode".

git grep '#1088' finds only two code comments, nothing a user sees, so closing the issue leaves no dangling pointer. Nothing from the issue is left undone.
